  "context": "6 of the 33 corrupt presentation clips found in eng_for_sin. 27 were linked to a real card (handled separately, NOT touched here). These 6 carry the same defect but their lego_id (S0181L03, S0181L04, S0197L03, S0198L03, S0202L03, S0204L02) does not exist in course_legos for eng_for_sin -- consistent with the presentation set having been composed against a LEGO numbering that has since been renumbered.",
  "verification_method": "For each row: (1) SELECT from course_legos WHERE course_code='eng_for_sin' AND lego_id = <lego_id> -- confirmed 0 rows for all 6. (2) SELECT from course_legos (any course_code) WHERE known_audio_id/target1_audio_id/target2_audio_id/presentation_audio_id = <this course_audio.id> -- confirmed 0 rows for all 6. (3) Swept every other table in the public schema with an *_audio_id / *_clip_id column (course_practice_phrases, course_seeds, lego_introductions, listening_pod_sentences, pod_legos, audio_clip_flags, audio_clip_signoffs, audio_clip_promotions, content_feedback, course_qa_cycle_clips, feedback_aggregated, course_audio_revisions, course_audio_envelope, audio_repair_candidates) -- all clean except course_qa_clip_status, which held one un-FK'd status row per id (QA tracking metadata about the clip itself, not a reference INTO the clip from course content -- confirmed via pg_constraint that no FK exists from course_qa_clip_status to course_audio).",
  "schema_note": "course_audio has NO status/deleted/archived column. CHECK constraint course_audio_role_check pins role to a fixed enum-like list (known/target1/target2/presentation/welcome/encouragement/instruction/bookend_listen_intro/bookend_listen_outro/pod_explainer/pod_fine_known/pod_take_g), so role cannot carry an 'archived' value. course_code has an FK to courses(course_code) ON DELETE CASCADE, so course_code cannot be repointed to a synthetic 'archived' value without that value existing in courses. The least-destructive available marker is lego_id, which has no FK and only a plain (non-unique) index -- prefixing it de-lists the row from any lego_id-keyed scan while leaving every other column, and the S3 object, untouched.",
  "soft_delete_marker": "lego_id prefixed with 'ARCHIVED_ORPHAN_2026-08-17_' (original value preserved after the prefix, and recorded verbatim in original_lego_id below)",
